 @justmixah3408  You grossly overestimate optimisation potential. Even games that are already made specifically for the PS5 (spiderman) cannot run at 60 fps with rt on. It doesn't even have many rt effects.

A console isn't just a gpu. It's a combination of many components, and the gpu is just one of them. The majority of the optimisations happening for the consoles are the result of the tightly integrated cpu and gpu, storage and combined vram+system memory. Most of them simply don't carry over to the pc. You also assume that the gpu inside the consoles is exactly the same as the discrete one, which couldn't be further from the truth. It's only based on rdna 2, but it's cut down, integrated onto the soc itself, and has sony's/msft's optimisation on top of it. The ps4 also had an amd gpu - based on gcn. Now think about how much it helped amd's desktop gcn offerings. x) 

You can keep having unrealistic expectations about the improvements it'll get from console optimisation, but get ready to be disappointed when pretty much none of it makes it to pcs.
